{"parentUuid":"b76e1e30-164b-4c7d-ad07-c835ed79211a","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a6480e76a7177e6fd","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01GU5pi4gaYH6pft1W66vTbd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NJtRqCZNgQ9ERQ7VrJ9ezg","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"\"certified optimal\" vs \"epsilon-optimal\" definition operations research industrial"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8195,"cache_read_input_tokens":13113,"output_tokens":435,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8195},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":435,"cache_read_input_tokens":13113,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8195,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8195,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoraYn1zifM8izUduDUR","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"4b7496dd-a076-42ef-bc85-bdef864d2d54","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:40:40.311Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"332b756e-9fa7-4b03-8e15-0ad69033cd96","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fa4d4bc6-e2b2-445f-8cd0-cc97f0106215","agentId":"a6480e76a7177e6fd","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SKv5LYk6PNnY1zyadpye13","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP-SAT OR-Tools absolute_gap_limit relative_gap_limit anytime solver bound certificate\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto\"},{\"title\":\"Setting solver limits | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_tasks\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"Coding Patterns - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/06_coding_patterns.html\"},{\"title\":\"Google OR-Tools: ortools.math_opt.python.parameters.SolveParameters Class Reference\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/python/classortools_1_1math__opt_1_1python_1_1parameters_1_1SolveParameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding the Log - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/understanding_the_log.html\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT, UNKNOWN status with complete solution hint · Issue #3750 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3750\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's information about CP-SAT's gap limit parameters and solver capabilities:\n\n## Gap Limit Parameters\n\nYou can specify acceptable solution quality using absolute_gap_limit and relative_gap_limit. The absolute limit stops the solver when the solution is within a specified value of the bound. The relative limit stops the solver when the objective value is within a specified ratio of the bound.\n\n## Technical Definitions\n\nThe solver stops the search when the gap between the best feasible objective and the best objective bound is smaller than a limit, with definitions being: Absolute: abs(O - B) and Relative: abs(O - B) / max(1, abs(O)). If the gap is reached, the search status will be OPTIMAL, but one can check the best objective bound to see the actual gap.\n\n## Anytime Solver Characteristics\n\nThe search progress log is essential for identifying performance bottlenecks and clearly demonstrates the solver's progression over time and pinpoints where it faces significant challenges. This demonstrates CP-SAT's anytime solver nature—it can be interrupted at any time and return the best feasible solution found so far.\n\n## Bounds and Certificates\n\nThe best_bound represents the proven bound on the objective function, i.e., the best possible value. This bound serves as a certificate of the solution quality during the search process.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"7332bbce-ec71-4838-8854-145b30f352f8","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:40:43.203Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"332b756e-9fa7-4b03-8e15-0ad69033cd96","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"8317f046-03c5-4c9b-8dc8-45add4c150d9","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fa4d4bc6-e2b2-445f-8cd0-cc97f0106215","agentId":"a6480e76a7177e6fd","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01S9RBzx6hGAFBLcsGVufr6m","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"OR-Tools CP-SAT BestObjectiveBound ObjectiveValue solution callback gap\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Accessing solver from BestBoundCallback in CP-SAT\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/SUwhJ3Favxg\"},{\"title\":\"Obtaining Intermediate Solutions in OR-Tools CP-SAT [Fixed]\",\"url\":\"https://www.technetexperts.com/ortools-intermediate-solutions-callback/\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"Searching for solutions close to optimal\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/R2d5PnYzH-o\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT solver returning non-optimal solutions with status \\\"OPTIMAL\\\" · Issue #3639 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3639\"},{\"title\":\"BestObjectiveBound - How to use it\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/V4GUqACoeKY\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/python/cp_model.py at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/python/cp_model.py\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"CP Sat is not optimizing my cost function · google/or-tools · Discussion #2491\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/2491\"}]\n\nI found relevant information about OR-Tools CP-SAT and the terms you searched for. Here's what the results show:\n\n## Key Concepts\n\n**BestObjectiveBound**: This provides the current proven lower bound (for minimization), which is useful for calculating the optimality gap in real-time within callbacks. It represents an optimistic approximation of the halfway-solved problem, and as the solver progresses, it proves that the previous approximation is unreachable and provides a potentially lower optimistic number.\n\n**ObjectiveValue**: This represents the objective value of the best feasible solution found so far.\n\n## Solution Callbacks\n\nThe CP-SAT solver provides a callback interface designed to monitor the search process, which is critical for tracking progress, logging metrics, or storing suboptimal but feasible results that satisfy all constraints before the global optimum is identified.\n\nWhen solving an optimization problem with an objective function, the CP-SAT solver internally adds a dynamic constraint. Every time a solution is found, the solver ensures that any subsequent solution must strictly improve the objective value. Consequently, the default on_solution_callback method is only triggered when a better solution is discovered.\n\n## Calculating the Optimality Gap\n\nYou can specify acceptable solution quality using absolute_gap_limit and relative_gap_limit. The absolute limit stops the solver when the solution is within a specified value of the bound. The relative limit stops the solver when the objective value is within a specified ratio of the bound.\n\nThe results also show discussions about using these values together in callbacks to implement advanced monitoring and early stopping strategies based on the optimality gap.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"08f145d4-e947-4d56-be15-f81c87cd26bb","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:40:45.343Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8317f046-03c5-4c9b-8dc8-45add4c150d9","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"f9c3af48-c0d7-42f0-ad5c-7faa73eb4940","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fa4d4bc6-e2b2-445f-8cd0-cc97f0106215","agentId":"a6480e76a7177e6fd","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ehy8hexEZSvScwKXViQ5Qy","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Gurobi MIPGap industrial practice 1% 5% supply chain optimization\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"What is the MIPGap? – Gurobi Help Center\",\"url\":\"https://support.gurobi.com/hc/en-us/articles/8265539575953-What-is-the-MIPGap\"},{\"title\":\"Gurobi: Mathematical Optimization for Complex Problems | DataCamp\",\"url\":\"https://www.datacamp.com/tutorial/gurobi\"},{\"title\":\"Optimization for the Supply Chain Industry | Gurobi\",\"url\":\"https://www.gurobi.com/industry/optimization-for-the-supply-chain-industry/\"},{\"title\":\"Relative MIP Gap in Gurobi's Branch and Bound | Download Scientific Diagram\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/figure/Relative-MIP-Gap-in-Gurobis-Branch-and-Bound_fig1_273670956\"},{\"title\":\"Mixed-Integer Programming (MIP) - Gurobi Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://www.gurobi.com/faqs/mixed-integer-programming/\"},{\"title\":\"Why does MIPGap not give me the actual optimality gap? – Gurobi Help Center\",\"url\":\"https://support.gurobi.com/hc/en-us/community/posts/16159579824273-Why-does-MIPGap-not-give-me-the-actual-optimality-gap\"},{\"title\":\"Parameter Guidelines - Gurobi Optimizer Reference Manual\",\"url\":\"https://docs.gurobi.com/projects/optimizer/en/current/concepts/parameters/guidelines.html\"},{\"title\":\"MIP Models - Gurobi Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://www.gurobi.com/documentation/9.5/refman/mip_models.html\"},{\"title\":\"How do I set multiple termination criteria for a model? – Gurobi Help Center\",\"url\":\"https://support.gurobi.com/hc/en-us/articles/360013419411-How-do-I-set-multiple-termination-criteria-for-a-model\"},{\"title\":\"Optimization for the Industrial Automation and Machinery Industry - Gurobi Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://www.gurobi.com/industry/optimization-for-the-industrial-automation-and-machinery-industry/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about Gurobi's MIPGap parameter and its industrial practice in supply chain optimization.\n\n## Key Findings:\n\n### MIPGap Parameter Basics\nThe MIPGap parameter controls the minimal quality of the returned solution and is an upper bound on the actual MIP gap of the final solution. The MIPGap parameter defines the relative optimality gap at which Gurobi will terminate the solve, with a default value of 0.0001 (0.01%).\n\n### Industrial Practice with 1% and 5% Gaps\nYou can set a \"MIPGap\" to stop the solver once it finds a solution within 1% or 5% of the optimal. For real-world decisions, a good answer now is often better than a perfect answer tomorrow.\n\n### Practical Rationale for Positive Gap Tolerances\nFor real-world applications, it is always sensible to set a positive MIP Gap tolerance since achieving an exact zero gap is often time-consuming and resource-intensive. That's why Gurobi by default uses a small, non-zero value for MIPGap to balance solution quality and solve time, providing near-optimal results without excessive computation. Smaller gaps lead to marginal solution improvements but require exponentially more effort.\n\n### Supply Chain Applications\nSupply chain optimization involves optimizing inventory distribution by accounting for demand variability, lead times, and transportation costs. Leading companies across numerous industries use Gurobi's mathematical optimization solver in a wide variety of applications to optimize their supply chain planning, decision making, and operations, and to keep supply and demand in balance.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"077caafc-e6e5-4fea-9555-e6ad668cfdf9","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:40:46.563Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f9c3af48-c0d7-42f0-ad5c-7faa73eb4940","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"4b7496dd-a076-42ef-bc85-bdef864d2d54","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fa4d4bc6-e2b2-445f-8cd0-cc97f0106215","agentId":"a6480e76a7177e6fd","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NJtRqCZNgQ9ERQ7VrJ9ezg","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"certified optimal\" vs \"epsilon-optimal\" definition operations research industrial\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Mastering Epsilon-Constraint Method\",\"url\":\"https://www.numberanalytics.com/blog/epsilon-constraint-method-operations-research\"},{\"title\":\"Operations research - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operations_research\"},{\"title\":\"Multiobjective optimization\",\"url\":\"https://openmdao.github.io/PracticalMDO/Notebooks/Optimization/multiobjective.html\"},{\"title\":\"EPSILON SOLUTIONS AND DUALITY IN VECTOR ...\",\"url\":\"https://pure.iiasa.ac.at/3009/1/WP-87-043.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"An Epsilon constraint-based evolutionary algorithm and multi-objective quality metrics for combined economic emission dispatch problem | Neural Computing and Applications | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00521-025-11330-2\"},{\"title\":\"An epsilon-constraint-based exact multi-objective optimization approach for the ship schedule recovery problem in liner shipping - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0360835223004965\"},{\"title\":\"Approximation algorithm - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Approximation_algorithm\"},{\"title\":\"Optimization - Operations Research Glossary\",\"url\":\"https://www.solvice.io/glossary/optimization\"},{\"title\":\"How to use the epsilon-constraint method? | ResearchGate\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/post/How-to-use-the-epsilon-constraint-method\"},{\"title\":\"Optimizing Decision-Making in AI: Fine-Tuning the Epsilon-Greedy Algorithm for Enhanced Performance | by Everton Gomede, PhD | Operations Research Bit | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/operations-research-bit/optimizing-decision-making-in-ai-fine-tuning-the-epsilon-greedy-algorithm-for-enhanced-performance-ea61e86d6f1d\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about the epsilon-constraint method in operations research, but the results primarily focus on the **epsilon-constraint method** (a technique for multi-objective optimization) rather than comparing \"certified optimal\" versus \"epsilon-optimal\" as distinct optimization concepts.\n\nLet me provide what I found:\n\n## Epsilon-Constraint Method in Operations Research\n\nThe epsilon-constraint method is a technique used in Operations Research to solve complex multi-objective optimization problems by optimizing one primary objective function while constraining the other objective functions to certain levels, denoted by ε (epsilon).\n\nThe method can handle non-convex problems and produce a more comprehensive set of Pareto-optimal solutions.\n\n## Epsilon-Optimality in Approximation Algorithms\n\nIn a related context, in computer science and operations research, approximation algorithms are efficient algorithms that find approximate solutions to optimization problems with provable guarantees on the distance of the returned solution to the optimal one. Some approximation algorithms can be approximated within a multiplicative factor ε > 0, producing solutions arbitrarily close to the optimum.\n\nThe search results did not return specific definitions contrasting \"certified optimal\" versus \"epsilon-optimal\" as distinct formal concepts in industrial operations research. If you're looking for more specific theoretical definitions of these terms, you may want to clarify whether you're referring to approximation theory, constraint-based optimization, or another specific OR subfield.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"b7db379b-82c1-4613-a5e5-26dd18584c4c","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:40:47.140Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4b7496dd-a076-42ef-bc85-bdef864d2d54","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
