Optimization 2025\",\"url\":\"https://www.cargese.org/2025/\"}]\n\nI've performed the web search for your query on bounded suboptimality, epsilon-optimal proof certificates, and combinatorial optimization from 2025. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Recent Work in Combinatorial Optimization (2025)\n\nThe search results reveal several relevant developments in 2025:\n\n### Approximation Algorithms with Predictions\nA systematic study has been initiated on utilizing predictions to improve over approximation guarantees of classic algorithms, without increasing the running time. The algorithms produce an optimal solution when provided with perfect predictions and their approximation ratio smoothly degrades with increasing prediction error.\n\n### Conference Proceedings\nA Polynomial Time Approximation Scheme (PTAS) has been developed for both the Boundary Cover and Corner Cover problems on simple polygons, using a local search algorithm, improving upon the previous best-known 4-approximation for the Boundary Cover and 2-approximation for the Corner Cover problems.\n\n### Bounded Suboptimality Concepts\nSolutions to approximate problems have provable suboptimality bounds under certain concavity conditions in the context of combinatorial dynamical systems optimization.\n\n### Recent Combinatorial Optimization Trends\nRecent developments in combinatorial optimization have seen advanced metaheuristic approaches and bi-criteria models that tackle problems with intricate conflict constraints, with novel bi-criteria strategies introduced in set covering problems where epsilon-constraint methods are employed.\n\nIf you're looking for more specific information about proof certificates or particular algorithmic approaches, feel free to ask for a more targeted search.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"a18a66cc-7293-4b2f-800b-b2c2b0e4a261","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:40:47.394Z","sourceToolAssistantUUI