{"parentUuid":"305bdea3-d29a-4b0c-9679-49b0e6673c9a","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a6480e76a7177e6fd","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01KbPKgnAz3vHF5puL3JqsD9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FDMs3uZStxGkzd1HkboC6D","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.CP.2025.21","prompt":"summarize: practically feasible proof logging for pseudo-Boolean optimization. What problems can be certified? Performance overhead vs solving? Is this applicable to CP-SAT optimization with epsilon gap?"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2521,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5895,"cache_read_input_tokens":27138,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5895,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":42,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaorcgQhv8LfS6L1LLwW6","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"84e3bc17-0ae6-417a-b5bd-0b474c934cdc","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:41:11.180Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"196014d8-9f3c-4df0-9902-a0787504d5ef","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fa4d4bc6-e2b2-445f-8cd0-cc97f0106215","agentId":"a6480e76a7177e6fd","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DH37j3XtB7We9QCGNUJCZP","type":"tool_result","content":"# CP-SAT Gap Limit Parameters and Termination\n\n## Parameter Names & Definitions\n\n**`relative_gap_limit`**: Halts solving when the objective value is within a specified ratio of the proven bound. The document states: \"To stop when the solution is (provably) within 5% of the optimum, use: `solver.parameters.relative_gap_limit = 0.05`\"\n\n**`absolute_gap_limit`**: Terminates when the solution is within a specified absolute value of the bound.\n\n## Code Examples\n\n```python\n# Set relative gap termination (5% tolerance)\nsolver.parameters.relative_gap_limit = 0.05\n\n# Set absolute gap termination\nsolver.parameters.absolute_gap_limit = 10\n```\n\n## Accessing Solution Quality Metrics\n\nThe solver provides two critical metrics within callbacks:\n\n```python\nclass MySolutionCallback(cp_model.CpSolverSolutionCallback):\n    def on_solution_callback(self):\n        obj = self.objective_value  # Best solution found\n        bound = self.best_objective_bound  # Best proven bound\n        gap = abs(obj - bound)\n```\n\n## Industrial Recommendations\n\n- **Time limits**: Start with 60-300 seconds for model testing\n- **Relative gap**: `0.05` (5% tolerance) balances optimality with runtime\n- **Anytime termination**: Combine time limits with gap limits for production systems\n\nThe primer emphasizes that bounds \"can be misleading\" and advises understanding their origin before relying on them as quality guarantees."}]},"uuid":"c0e7105a-c591-46b0-b9b9-542f2a0db3d3","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:41:11.517Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"196014d8-9f3c-4df0-9902-a0787504d5ef","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"c0e7105a-c591-46b0-b9b9-542f2a0db3d3","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a6480e76a7177e6fd","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01KbPKgnAz3vHF5puL3JqsD9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VB3BFnaD5Gjum7UevcPsms","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/Yra_AIJ3kkE","prompt":"extract the discussion: how to set optimality tolerance in CP-SAT, what status is returned when gap_limit is hit, code samples"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2521,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5895,"cache_read_input_tokens":27138,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5895,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":42,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaorcgQhv8LfS6L1LLwW6","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"432a3aa3-0c06-4634-ad0d-0220515771d6","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:41:12.889Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"432a3aa3-0c06-4634-ad0d-0220515771d6","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fa4d4bc6-e2b2-445f-8cd0-cc97f0106215","agentId":"a6480e76a7177e6fd","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VB3BFnaD5Gjum7UevcPsms","type":"tool_result","content":"# Discussion Summary: Optimality Tolerance in CP-SAT/SCIP\n\n## Question\nVijay Gupta asked: \"How can I set the optimality tolerance?\" for solvers like CP-SAT/SCIP, in addition to implementing a time limit.\n\n## Answer Provided\nLaurent Perron responded by referencing a Stack Overflow discussion on \"how to combine time and gap limits with google or-tools in python,\" noting that he had provided specific guidance about SAT solver configuration in a comment on that thread.\n\n## Key Points\n- The discussion addresses combining multiple stopping criteria (time limits and optimality tolerance/gap limits)\n- The solution involves using gap limit parameters in OR-Tools\n- Specific implementation details were provided in an external Stack Overflow reference rather than in this group message\n\n**Note:** The actual code samples and detailed technical specifications about what status is returned when gap limits are reached were not included in the excerpted content shown here—they appear to be in the referenced Stack Overflow discussion."}]},"uuid":"5cd65167-0aff-4acd-9759-04941efc0518","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:41:17.998Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"432a3aa3-0c06-4634-ad0d-0220515771d6","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"84e3bc17-0ae6-417a-b5bd-0b474c934cdc","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fa4d4bc6-e2b2-445f-8cd0-cc97f0106215","agentId":"a6480e76a7177e6fd","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FDMs3uZStxGkzd1HkboC6D","type":"tool_result","content":"# Practically Feasible Proof Logging for Pseudo-Boolean Optimization\n\n## Overview\nThis paper presents an efficient toolchain for formally verified pseudo-Boolean optimization, implementing proof logging in state-of-the-art solvers RoundingSat and Sat4j.\n\n## Certifiable Problems\nThe work covers \"the full range of techniques in the state-of-the-art solvers,\" including:\n- Core-guided search\n- Linear programming integration with Farkas certificates\n- Cut generation\n\nThis extends certification beyond decision problems to optimization tasks involving 0-1 integer linear programming.\n\n## Performance Overhead\nThe research demonstrates that \"proof logging and checking performance in this much more expressive paradigm is now quite close to the level of SAT solving, and hence is clearly practically feasible.\" The experimental evaluation shows the overhead is manageable for real-world deployment.\n\n## Applicability to CP-SAT with Epsilon Gap\n**The document does not address CP-SAT or epsilon-gap optimization.** The work focuses on exact pseudo-Boolean optimization with formal verification, not approximate solving methods. There is no discussion of tolerance-based solution verification or approximate optimization paradigms.\n\nTo determine whether these techniques apply to CP-SAT's epsilon-gap approach would require examining CP-SAT's specific architecture and certification requirements—information not contained in this paper."}]},"uuid":"a62dcc7c-d918-4e68-af13-8026e25ca5d9","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:41:18.239Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"84e3bc17-0ae6-417a-b5bd-0b474c934cdc","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
