{"parentUuid":"c4359e0f-7bd1-4489-bab5-14acea11d8ab","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a6480e76a7177e6fd","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01LMG12rnzC5BfdakLL4atJc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Y9y2mX8qbeUJy83CTSsvdL","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"\"primal-dual gap\" optimization certificate audit large-scale industrial deployment LBBD"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":374,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4261,"cache_read_input_tokens":33033,"output_tokens":426,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4261},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":374,"output_tokens":426,"cache_read_input_tokens":33033,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4261,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4261,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaordtGd7yhw91P8wN8bj","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"0827cbad-920a-4c56-b581-f8855dbcbb02","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:41:25.051Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"05b8e567-0f4e-44c7-966c-24bca65d69f9","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fa4d4bc6-e2b2-445f-8cd0-cc97f0106215","agentId":"a6480e76a7177e6fd","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VCvGdsi5MMzv4rWUo2XRJY","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP-SAT status FEASIBLE OPTIMAL relative_gap_limit reached returns which status\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT solver returning non-optimal solutions with status \\\"OPTIMAL\\\" · Issue #3639 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3639\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT, UNKNOWN status with complete solution hint · Issue #3750 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3750\"},{\"title\":\"CpSolverStatus in cp_sat::proto - Rust\",\"url\":\"https://docs.rs/cp_sat/latest/cp_sat/proto/enum.CpSolverStatus.html\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding the Log - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/understanding_the_log.html\"},{\"title\":\"SCIP Solver returns solution as OPTIMAL when it isn't · Issue #3672 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3672\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools: ortools/sat/docs/troubleshooting.md | Fossies\",\"url\":\"https://fossies.org/linux/or-tools/ortools/sat/docs/troubleshooting.md\"},{\"title\":\"Coding Patterns - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/06_coding_patterns.html\"},{\"title\":\"order of constraints changes cp-sat outcome from feasible to infeasible · Issue #4168 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/4168\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I can provide you with information about CP-SAT solver status returns:\n\nWhen the `relative_gap_limit` is reached, CP-SAT returns an OPTIMAL status. More specifically, if a gap limit has been specified and the solver returns a solution within this limit, it returns OPTIMAL.\n\nTo clarify the different status values that CP-SAT can return: The status can be FEASIBLE, OPTIMAL, INFEASIBLE, UNKNOWN, or MODEL_INVALID.\n\nSo when `relative_gap_limit` is reached, the solver returns **OPTIMAL** status, not FEASIBLE. This indicates that while the solution may not be provably optimal in the strictest mathematical sense, it is within the specified optimality gap tolerance you set, which is considered a success by CP-SAT's definition.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"8b070e8f-42a8-4930-a6af-c85f4268839c","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:41:28.707Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"05b8e567-0f4e-44c7-966c-24bca65d69f9","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"908667f1-a942-42d7-bdbe-130fd6ede095","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fa4d4bc6-e2b2-445f-8cd0-cc97f0106215","agentId":"a6480e76a7177e6fd","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015m2fAw9fHWXjx7Kj54fDN8","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"Amazon\" OR \"DHL\" OR \"UPS\" OR \"FedEx\" Gurobi MIP gap production solution optimal\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"What is the MIPGap? – Gurobi Help Center\",\"url\":\"https://support.gurobi.com/hc/en-us/articles/8265539575953-What-is-the-MIPGap\"},{\"title\":\"Amazon takes aim at the supply chain\",\"url\":\"https://www.axios.com/2026/05/05/amazon-logistics-ups-fedex\"},{\"title\":\"Is it possible to change when (the gap %level) Gurobi starts focusing on finding feasible solutions instead finding a lower lower bound? – Gurobi Help Center\",\"url\":\"https://support.gurobi.com/hc/en-us/community/posts/20206323134353-Is-it-possible-to-change-when-the-gap-level-Gurobi-starts-focusing-on-finding-feasible-solutions-instead-finding-a-lower-lower-bound\"},{\"title\":\"Amazon Launches “Amazon Supply Chain Services” to Take on UPS and FedEx in U.S. Logistics Market\",\"url\":\"https://www.logisticsinsider.in/amazon-launches-amazon-supply-chain-services-to-take-on-ups-and-fedex-in-u-s-logistics-market/\"},{\"title\":\"Optimization for the Supply Chain Industry | Gurobi\",\"url\":\"https://www.gurobi.com/industry/optimization-for-the-supply-chain-industry/\"},{\"title\":\"Amazon Opens Logistics Network To All Businesses And Challenges UPS And FedEx - Simply Wall St News\",\"url\":\"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/retail/nasdaq-amzn/amazoncom/news/amazon-opens-logistics-network-to-all-businesses-and-challen/amp\"},{\"title\":\"Amazon turns its logistics empire into a new business, taking on UPS and FedEx in freight and shipping – GeekWire\",\"url\":\"https://www.geekwire.com/2026/amazon-turns-its-logistics-empire-into-a-new-business-taking-on-ups-and-fedex-in-freight-and-shipping/\"},{\"title\":\"2025 Guide for Ecommerce Shipping Carriers - UPS, USPS, FedEx, DHL\",\"url\":\"https://www.atomixlogistics.com/blog/ecommerce-shipping-carriers-ups-usps-fedex-dhl\"},{\"title\":\"Amazon Supply Chain Services Opens Its Logistics Network to Everybody: Should DHL, UPS, and FedEx Worry? – CityLogistics\",\"url\":\"https://www.citylogistics.info/business/amazon-supply-chain-services-opens-its-logistics-network-to-everybody-should-dhl-ups-and-fedex-worry/\"},{\"title\":\"Amazon Challenges UPS and FedEx by Opening Global Logistics Network to All Businesses | AlphaPilot\",\"url\":\"https://www.alphapilot.tech/discover/amazon-challenges-ups-and-fedex-by-opening-global-logistics-network-to-all-businesses\"}]\n\nI found search results related to your query. The results contain information about:\n\n1. **Gurobi MIP Gap Concepts**: The MIPGap parameter controls the minimal quality of the returned solution and is an upper bound on the actual MIP gap of the final solution. Gurobi by default uses a small, non-zero value for MIPGap to balance solution quality and solve time, providing near-optimal results without excessive computation.\n\n2. **Supply Chain Competition**: The search results also include recent information about Amazon, UPS, FedEx, and DHL in the logistics industry. Amazon announced on May 4, 2026, the launch of Amazon Supply Chain Services (ASCS), a new initiative that opens its massive internal logistics and delivery infrastructure to any business worldwide.\n\nHowever, the search results do not contain specific information connecting these four logistics companies (Amazon, DHL, UPS, FedEx) with Gurobi optimization for MIP gap production solutions. The results show general Gurobi MIP documentation and recent logistics market news, but not a case study or specific implementation combining all these elements. \n\nIf you're looking for specific case studies or technical documentation about how these logistics companies use Gurobi for production optimization, you may need to search more specifically or check directly with Gurobi's case studies or industry publications.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"e455cedc-0a4a-4681-83c4-445f83914435","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:41:29.129Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"908667f1-a942-42d7-bdbe-130fd6ede095","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"89b3774d-5b8b-4ae1-b0af-490c603db39c","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fa4d4bc6-e2b2-445f-8cd0-cc97f0106215","agentId":"a6480e76a7177e6fd","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Qk5h11PnK2n1rWkz1NddWP","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Gurobi MIPGap default 0.0001 industrial solver scheduling vehicle routing 1% 5% acceptable\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"What is the MIPGap? – Gurobi Help Center\",\"url\":\"https://support.gurobi.com/hc/en-us/articles/8265539575953-What-is-the-MIPGap\"},{\"title\":\"Parameter Guidelines - Gurobi Optimizer Reference Manual\",\"url\":\"https://docs.gurobi.com/projects/optimizer/en/current/concepts/parameters/guidelines.html\"},{\"title\":\"Why does MIPGap not give me the actual optimality gap? – Gurobi Help Center\",\"url\":\"https://support.gurobi.com/hc/en-us/community/posts/16159579824273-Why-does-MIPGap-not-give-me-the-actual-optimality-gap\"},{\"title\":\"Parameter Reference - Gurobi Optimizer Reference Manual\",\"url\":\"https://docs.gurobi.com/projects/optimizer/en/current/reference/parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"About the MIPgap – Gurobi Help Center\",\"url\":\"https://support.gurobi.com/hc/en-us/community/posts/4406142530961-About-the-MIPgap\"},{\"title\":\"GUROBI Options — AMPL Resources\",\"url\":\"https://dev.ampl.com/solvers/gurobi/options.html\"},{\"title\":\"Objectives - Gurobi Optimizer Reference Manual\",\"url\":\"https://docs.gurobi.com/projects/optimizer/en/current/concepts/modeling/objectives.html\"},{\"title\":\"How to have a solution with 0 gap – Gurobi Help Center\",\"url\":\"https://support.gurobi.com/hc/en-us/community/posts/360077631972-How-to-have-a-solution-with-0-gap\"},{\"title\":\"Getting Stuck in gap in MIP optimization model – Gurobi Help Center\",\"url\":\"https://support.gurobi.com/hc/en-us/community/posts/20856079255441-Getting-Stuck-in-gap-in-MIP-optimization-model\"},{\"title\":\"MIP Models - Gurobi Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://www.gurobi.com/documentation/9.1/refman/mip_models.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's the information about Gurobi's MIPGap parameter:\n\n## Default MIPGap Value\n\nThe default value of the MIPGap parameter is 0.0001 (0.01%).\n\n## How MIPGap Works\n\nMIPGap is a common termination choice for MIP models that allows you to indicate that optimization should stop when the relative gap between the best known solution and the best known bound on the solution objective is less than the specified value.\n\n## Practical Gap Tolerances\n\nFor industrial applications like scheduling and vehicle routing problems, you can set different tolerances:\n\n- If you set a MIPGap of 1%, Gurobi will return an optimal solution with a final MIPGap ≤ 1%, and it is possible that the optimal solution has a MIPGap of <0.001% or even 0%.\n- A 5% MIPGap tolerance would be more relaxed, allowing faster solve times but accepting solutions with larger optimality gaps.\n\n## Balancing Solution Quality and Speed\n\nGurobi by default uses a small, non-zero value for MIPGap to balance solution quality and solve time, providing near-optimal results without excessive computation. For discrete models, it is more common to stop when the solution objective is within a specified gap from the optimal value, controlled by the MIPGap parameter with a default value of 0.01%.\n\nFor industrial problems like vehicle routing and scheduling, tolerances of 1-5% are often considered acceptable depending on your specific business requirements and time constraints.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"ef7d777c-ba01-4abb-b91e-767f9efadeaf","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:41:29.730Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"89b3774d-5b8b-4ae1-b0af-490c603db39c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"c4359e0f-7bd1-4489-bab5-14acea11d8ab","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fa4d4bc6-e2b2-445f-8cd0-cc97f0106215","agentId":"a6480e76a7177e6fd","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VHjQ9mzd2kjdc15t2ceh7q","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"VeriPB CP-SAT proof logging optimality certificate 2025 OR-tools\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"VeriPB Proof Checking Toolchain\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/veripb-proof-checking-toolchain\"},{\"title\":\"Practically Feasible Proof Logging for Pseudo-Boolean Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol340-cp2025/html/LIPIcs.CP.2025.21/LIPIcs.CP.2025.21.html\"},{\"title\":\"Pseudo Boolean Competition 2025\",\"url\":\"http://www.cril.univ-artois.fr/PB25/\"},{\"title\":\"A Multi-Stage Proof Logging Framework to Certify the Correctness of CP Solvers\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol307-cp2024/LIPIcs.CP.2024.11/LIPIcs.CP.2024.11.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding the Log - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/understanding_the_log.html\"},{\"title\":\"enable the log of CP-SAT solver · google/or-tools · Discussion #3873\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/3873\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools: ortools/sat/docs/troubleshooting.md | Fossies\",\"url\":\"https://fossies.org/linux/or-tools/ortools/sat/docs/troubleshooting.md\"},{\"title\":\"Pseudo-Boolean Proof Logging for Optimal Classical Planning\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2504.18443\"},{\"title\":\"Documentation of VeriPB and CakePB for the SAT Competition 2025 Markus Anders\",\"url\":\"https://jakobnordstrom.se/docs/publications/DocumentationVeriPBandCakePBforSATcompetition2025.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about VeriPB, proof logging, and optimality certificates in the 2025 context:\n\n## Key Findings\n\n**VeriPB Proof Logging for Optimization:**\n\nVeriPB is a pseudo-Boolean proof system that, together with the formally verified backend CakePB, provides a toolchain for linear pseudo-Boolean optimization with fully formally verified conclusions, and represents the first certified solving toolchain for an optimization problem beyond SAT with performance approaching that of SAT proof logging tools.\n\n**2025 Updates and Developments:**\n\nRecent developments in VeriPB include support for multi-objective MaxSAT with Pareto-optimality and symmetry breaking, as documented in work from January and November 2025.\n\n**Pseudo-Boolean Competition 2025:**\n\nThe 2025 Pseudo Boolean Competition includes tracks for PB Optimization (PBO) where certificates of optimality must be generated in the VeriPB format. VeriPB proof logging is used to certify not only unsatisfiability but also satisfiability and optimality.\n\n**Relation to OR-Tools CP-SAT:**\n\nWhile the search results show information about Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT solver, they don't reveal direct integration of VeriPB proof logging with CP-SAT. The results do show that CP-SAT supports extensive logging capabilities, but no specific mention of VeriPB-format optimality certificate generation from CP-SAT was found in these results.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"7e4cc10c-a802-4ee9-9c26-ec5f282bc55c","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:41:31.100Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c4359e0f-7bd1-4489-bab5-14acea11d8ab","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"0827cbad-920a-4c56-b581-f8855dbcbb02","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fa4d4bc6-e2b2-445f-8cd0-cc97f0106215","agentId":"a6480e76a7177e6fd","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Y9y2mX8qbeUJy83CTSsvdL","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"primal-dual gap\" optimization certificate audit large-scale industrial deployment LBBD\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Self-Certifying Primal-Dual Optimization Proxies for Large-Scale Batch Economic Dispatch\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2510.15850v1\"},{\"title\":\"[2510.15850] Self-Certifying Primal-Dual Optimization Proxies for Large-Scale Batch Economic Dispatch\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.15850\"},{\"title\":\"Primal-Dual Rates and Certiﬁcates Celestine D¨unner CDU@ZURICH.IBM.COM\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1602.05205\"},{\"title\":\"Primal–Dual Methods for Large-Scale and Distributed Convex Optimization and Data Analytics | IEEE Journals & Magazine | IEEE Xplore\",\"url\":\"https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/9151295/\"},{\"title\":\"Primal-Dual Optimization Perspective\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/primal-dual-optimization-perspective\"},{\"title\":\"Practical Large-Scale Linear Programming using Primal- ...\",\"url\":\"https://proceedings.neurips.cc/paper/2021/file/a8fbbd3b11424ce032ba813493d95ad7-Paper.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Practical Large-Scale Linear Programming using Primal-Dual Hybrid Gradient\",\"url\":\"https://papers.neurips.cc/paper_files/paper/2021/file/a8fbbd3b11424ce032ba813493d95ad7-Paper.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"[1602.05205] Primal-Dual Rates and Certificates\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1602.05205\"},{\"title\":\"Infeasibility Detection with Primal-Dual Hybrid Gradient for Large-Scale Linear Programming | SIAM Journal on Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://epubs.siam.org/doi/abs/10.1137/22M1510467\"},{\"title\":\"Playing with Duality: An Overview of Recent Primal-Dual ...\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1406.5429\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about primal-dual gap optimization certificates and their deployment:\n\n## Key Research Areas\n\n**Self-Certifying Optimization Proxies for Industrial Deployment:**\n\nRecent work combines primal and dual feasible solutions to provide a self-contained mathematical certificate of performance in the form of a provable duality gap. When the duality gap of a predicted primal-dual solution exceeds a user-prescribed optimality tolerance, the corresponding instance is solved exactly using a classical optimization solver, ensuring worst-case optimality guarantees while providing large overall speedup since only a small fraction of samples exhibit poor performance.\n\n**Industrial Application - Batch Economic Dispatch:**\n\nFor large-scale transmission systems, the hybrid solver achieves speedups of over 1000x compared to a parallelized simplex-based solver while guaranteeing a maximum optimality gap of 2%.\n\n**Algorithmic Frameworks:**\n\nAlgorithm-independent frameworks equip existing optimization methods with primal-dual certificates, which are important for practitioners to diagnose progress, particularly in machine learning applications. These approaches provide efficiently computable duality gaps which are globally defined, without modifying the original problems in the region of interest.\n\n**Broader Applications:**\n\nPrimal-dual methodology has been broadly adopted across machine learning, signal processing, engineering, and control due to its robustness, versatility, mathematical transparency, and amenability to parallelization.\n\nThe search results primarily focus on theoretical frameworks and applications to economic dispatch problems, with limited direct information about LBBD (Logic-Based Benders Decomposition) specifically.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"0538c3fc-e387-49f2-992c-aec0fb54c19c","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:41:32.679Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0827cbad-920a-4c56-b581-f8855dbcbb02","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
